  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Case Study: An innovative proposal for education transformation in vulnerable contexts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Social Model for Strengthening Educational Communities, is an initiative of the Alberto Baill&#xe8;res Foundation, following the 2017 earthquakes in Mexico. Its intention is to promote education in vulnerable areas through the construction of educational habitats. This concept integrates innovative and high-quality infrastructure, and the generation of socio-community processes involving the entire community. Since 2019, UNESCO Mexico has provided technical assistance for the development and consolidation of the model, showcasing evidence to contribute to SDG 4 and the 2030 Agenda. The purpose is to expand collaboration, consolidate the Model and develop the rural chapter.</narrative>
  </description>
